[signal arg="spot:none"]
Your Grace, I am your Hand. Let me show you how the realm answers to you.
- I know the realm
	[end_timeline]
- Show me
[signal arg="do:select"]
This is your host. Click it.
[signal arg="do:march"]
Now right-click open ground. Your host marches there.
[signal arg="spot:none"]
Well done. Press A before you click, and it falls on any foe it meets on the road.
[signal arg="do:houses"]
These are the great houses. Open them.
[signal arg="spot:houses"]
Swear a house to you and its men fight your wars. A gift or a feast warms a cold lord.
War takes their towns one by one, their seat last. Every house remembers what you do to one of them.
[signal arg="spot:chronicle"]
This is your chronicle. Only what needs you stands here, the gravest first, one new matter at a time.
[signal arg="do:answer"]
Here is a matter for you. The answer on the right is the one I would give. Choose one.
[signal arg="spot:pause"]
Pause whenever you need to think. Your orders still go out.
[signal arg="spot:none"]
Nothing guards a town but its own men and your hosts. When raiders come, answer, or it burns.
The realm is yours, Your Grace. Press the question mark above whenever you want me again.
